# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The guest kernel has no ashmem and the product sets sys.use_memfd, and the
# vendor policy enables memfd_class, so the shared buffers an application
# creates are memfd files labelled with the application's domain. A MediaCodec
# queues its encrypted input in such a buffer (EncryptedLinearInputBuffers) and
# the ClearKey HAL maps it to decrypt into it. The platform grants a HAL access
# to the buffers of its declared clients and to file descriptors from
# applications, but not to the memfd files of applications, so every decrypt of
# a ClearKey stream failed on a denied read, write and map. Only the ClearKey HAL
# gets the rule: hal_drm_server also covers the Widevine HAL of the system. An
# isolated application never reaches a DRM HAL.
allow hal_drm_clearkey_aidl { appdomain -isolated_app_all }:memfd_file { getattr map read write };
